# Propagators

Here we try to see what implementing [propagators](https://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/users/gjs/6.945/readings/art.pdf) in Dialang.
I got introduced to propagator programming through [this conference](https://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/users/gjs/6.945/readings/art.pdf).

This is about solving complex problems under constraints.

*/

Assume(v) := (Id(Assumption), v)

Node(a, b, c)
  := ( .compute:
          ( .a: (b, c) -> a
          , .b: (c, a) -> b
          , .c: (a, b) -> c
          )
     , .resolve:
          ( .a: List(a) -> a
          , .b: List(b) -> b
          , .c: List(c) -> c
          )
     , .assumptions:
          List(Assume([a|b|c]))
     )

PortId(v)
  := { #a(Id(Node(v, _, _)))
     | #b(Id(Node(_, v, _)))
     | #c(Id(Node(_, _, v)))
     }

BiDict(node)
  := d:Dict(node,node)
     with l = Dict.to_list(d)
     where List.isUnique(List.map({(a,b)->(b,a)}, l) ++ l)

IdDict(v) := Dict(Id(v), v)

Id(v) := #id Int

Assumption := (PortId(v), v)

Graph
  := ( edges : BiDict(PortId(_))
     , nodes : IdDict(Node(_,_,_))
     , assume : IdDict(Assumption)
     )
